Deploy soluzione poc-powershell-dispatch (Asset-Terminator)

1) Prerequisiti
- Azure CLI + Azure Functions Core Tools (func) + Bicep.
- Ruolo Owner sul Resource Group dedicato (lo script crea role assignment RBAC:
  con il solo ruolo Contributor il deploy fallisce).
- App registration Entra con permessi applicativi su Microsoft Graph
  (DeviceManagementManagedDevices.Read.All, admin consent) e un certificato
  app-only per l'autenticazione dei runbook.

2) Comando di deploy
  cd poc-powershell-dispatch/infra
  ./deploy.ps1 -ResourceGroup ASSET-TERMINATOR-DISPATCH-RG `
     -Subscription <subscription-id> -Location westeurope `
     -GraphTenantId <tenant> -GraphClientId <appId> -GraphClientSecret <secret>

Parametri: ResourceGroup (obbl.), Subscription, Location (def westeurope),
NamePrefix (def attdisp), Env (def dev), GraphTenantId/GraphClientId/
GraphClientSecret (obbl.), -SkipPublish (ferma dopo infra + runbook).
Nota: GraphClientSecret e' usato SOLO dalla Function API per i lookup
read-only del device su Graph. I runbook preferiscono il certificato e usano
ClientSecret solo come fallback opzionale se l'autenticazione con certificato
non e' disponibile.

3) Cosa fa lo script
- Provisiona l'infrastruttura (main.bicep): 2 Function App, Service Bus,
  Automation Account, App Insights, runtime PowerShell 7.4, tabella di stato,
  private endpoint, role assignment e le Automation Variables.
- Sincronizza i moduli condivisi (build.ps1) e pubblica le due Function App.
- Carica e pubblica i 3 runbook RBK-WindowsDisposal / RBK-AppleDisposal /
  RBK-AndroidDisposal.

4) Automation Variables
Create e valorizzate dal bicep: ClientId, TenantId, GraphCertificateName
(GraphAppCert), AppInsightsConnectionString.
Create vuote e cifrate, da valorizzare dopo il deploy: Certificate_thumbprint,
ClientSecret (opzionale, fallback), ABM-ClientId, ABM-KeyId, ABM-PrivateKey,
KME-ClientIdentifier, KME-KeysJson, KME-CustomerId.
Certificato Graph: caricare l'asset GraphAppCert (Automation Certificate).
Auth runbook: certificato (GraphAppCert) -> thumbprint (cert store) ->
client secret (ClientSecret) come ultimo fallback.

  az automation variable update -g ASSET-TERMINATOR-DISPATCH-RG `
    --automation-account-name attdisp-auto-dev `
    --name Certificate_thumbprint --value '"<thumbprint>"' --encrypted true

  az automation variable update -g ASSET-TERMINATOR-DISPATCH-RG `
    --automation-account-name attdisp-auto-dev `
    --name ClientSecret --value '"<client-secret>"' --encrypted true

  az automation certificate create -g ASSET-TERMINATOR-DISPATCH-RG `
    --automation-account-name attdisp-auto-dev `
    --name GraphAppCert --path ./graph-app.pfx --password '<pfx-password>'

5) Verifica post-deploy
- Recuperare la function key (WipeIntake) e inviare una richiesta con dryRun=true.
- Controllare i customEvents su App Insights e il Workbook "Asset-Terminator -
  Wipe Requests".

